      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/domain/trade-analysis/derive.ts",
      "content": "After X2 consumes all lots this still returns a one-element positions array, while `derive` determines lifecycle solely from `positions.length \u003e 0`. Thus a fully exited trade is reported as Open, and a stored Closed lifecycle produces a false disagreement. Update lifecycle derivation to distinguish no executions (Planned), remaining exposure (Open), and fully disposed exposure (Closed); merely dropping the empty position would currently label it Planned.",
      "existing_code": "    positions: [\n      {\n        instrument: facts[0]!.instrument,\n        quantity: lots.reduce((sum, l) =\u003e sum.add(l.quantity), Rational.of(0n)),\n        openLots: lots,\n      },\n    ],",
      "start_line": 390,
